        "body": "## Why\n\nThe managed-layer API has two semantic tiers with different precedence. Their provenance must be representable consistently before the loader starts producing them, so diagnostics and public config inspection do not collapse them into the legacy enterprise source.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add `CloudManagedLayer::{Baseline, SystemOverlay}`\n- add cloud-managed config and requirements provenance with explicit tier, id, and name\n- map the additive source through diagnostics, hooks, app-server v2, and the TUI debug-config view\n- assign baseline precedence below local system/MDM and system-overlay precedence between system and user\n- keep all legacy enterprise variants intact\n\nNo bundle producer emits these sources in this PR.\n\n## Stack\n\n2 of 4. Stacked on #31285. Next: #31287.\n\n## Validation\n\n- regenerated app-server schemas, including experimental fixtures\n- focused config, app-server mapping, hooks, and TUI snapshot coverage\n- scoped Clippy fixes and repository formatting",
