        "body": "## Why\n\nThe loader needs a reviewable, independently reversible representation of both managed tiers before the backend/cache cutover. Keeping this step additive preserves the current enterprise producer while making precedence and provenance testable in isolation.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add managed `baseline` and `system_overlay` buckets for config and requirements\n- reverse backend high-to-low fragment order within each bucket into stack merge order\n- place config as baseline \u2192 system \u2192 legacy enterprise \u2192 system overlay \u2192 user\n- place requirements as baseline \u2192 system \u2192 legacy enterprise \u2192 system overlay \u2192 legacy/admin\n- emit the cloud-managed provenance introduced by #31286\n- omit empty managed buckets from the existing v1 cache representation\n\nExisting enterprise bundle behavior remains intact in this PR.\n\n## Stack\n\n3 of 5. Stacked on #31286. Runtime cutover: #31288. Cleanup: #31315.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-config -p codex-cloud-config` (232 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-config`\n- independent staged-diff review found no actionable issues\n",
